From 822b85664a67fceb42e1d32b906ae633e5e95597 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (sandbox)" <claude@sandbox.local>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 10:11:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Cohort assembly prep: persist obligation resolution
 fields, ship domain in the clear

Two prerequisite fixes for cohort assembly (C2 dimensions 4+5), found by
reading the real repo rather than assuming the handoff doc's scope:

1. The twin's obligation_ledger computed favorable/resolved_value/
   resolved_at/resolution_provenance/resolution_method on every RESOLVED
   transition but never wrote them to the database or the hash chain --
   the twin could say an obligation was RESOLVED but not how. Now
   persisted and hashed in (resolution fields only enter the hash when
   present, so an OPEN row's hash is unaffected).

2. domain is now shipped in the clear from primary to twin, alongside
   the existing outcome_obligation/decided_at fields, parsed from
   cassette_version's fixed domain:name:version format via the new
   domain_from_cassette_version() helper. Previously the twin only knew
   obligation_kind, and silently conflated it with domain -- two
   unrelated cassettes choosing the same obligation_kind string would
   have merged cohorts that have no business being compared. domain is
   a required field on every obligation from this point forward (not an
   optional backward-compat addition like the resolution fields), with a
   safe fallback to obligation_kind for entries shipped before this fix.

18 new tests. Full suite 557 passed / 6 skipped (544 baseline + 13 net
new -- some new tests replace/rename a prior test). ruff and bandit
clean.
